Buenos Aires, Argentina","California, USA","170 cm","Brooklyn, New York, USA","Toronto, Ontario, Canada","Munich, Germany","Tokyo, Japan",1980,"5'' 10 1/2\"","Boston, Massachusetts, USA","Detroit, Michigan, USA","6'' 0\"","Washington, District of Columbia, USA","173 cm","Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","England, UK","Mexico City, Distrito Federal, Mexico","New York, USA","St. Louis, Missouri, USA","Stockholm, Sweden","175 cm","5'' 7 1/2\"","5'' 8 1/2\"","5'' 9 1/2\"","6'' 5\"","Belgrade, Serbia, Yugoslavia","Copenhagen, Denmark","Hollywood, California, USA","Houston, Texas, USA","Vienna, Austria","180 cm","5'' 1\"","5'' 5 1/2\"","Cleveland, Ohio, USA","Helsinki, Finland",Hungary,"Los Angeles County, California, USA","Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA","Rio de Janeiro, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil","Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden","160 cm","168 cm","172 cm","183 cm",1952,1974,"6'' 2 1/2\"","6'' 6\"","Hamburg, Germany","Lisbon, Portugal","Madrid, Spain","Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA","Santa Monica, California, USA","182 cm",1950,1959,5'',"6'' 1 1/2\"","Istanbul, Turkey","165 cm","178 cm",1958,1966,1968,1972,"5'' 11 1/2\"","San Diego, California, USA","Seattle, Washington, USA","163 cm","185 cm",1973}', 'text'::regtype, -1), array_in('{"\"\"Monsters and Heroes\"\" (USA), March, 1968, Vol. 1, Iss. 3, pg. 26-34, by: Larry Ivie, \"\"Heroes of TV - The Three Faces of Captain Video\"\"","\"Celebrity Sleuth\" (USA), 1991, Vol. 4, Iss. 8, pg. 88-93, by: staff, \"The 25 Sexiest Women of 1992 - #2\"","\"Denver Post\" (USA), 3 May 2011, pg. entertainment section, by: John Wenzel, \"Successful and potty-mouthed, Chelsea Handler takes on the boys club Read more: Successful and potty-mouthed, Chelsea Handler takes on the boys club\"","\"Frontiers Magazine\" (USA), 8 April 2008, Vol. 26, Iss. 24, pg. Cover, 10 & 39, by: Jeremy Kinser, \"25 Great Things about L.A.\"","\"International Herald Tribune\" (USA), 30 June 2004, Iss. 37731, pg. 9, by: David Stevens, \"Summer of Strauss and farewells\"","\"Milliyet\" (Turkey), 19 March 2005, by: Elif Berkoz, \"Niyetim olsaydi antrenörüm beni boksör yapacakti\"","\"Oui\" (USA), April 1981, Vol. 10, Iss. 4, pg. 56-59, by: Michael Schumacher, \"Royko: Journalism''s No. 1 Tough Guy\"","\"Playboy\" (USA), November 1991, Vol. 38, Iss. 11, pg. 32, by: Bruce Williamson, \"Off Camera: Christopher Hart\"","\"Screen\" (UK), 14 May 2005, pg. 10, by: Liz Shackleton, \"Wong climbs on Hippopotamus Films'' Jessica\"","\"TV Guide\" (USA), 26 October 2009, Vol. 57, Iss. 43, pg. 38-39, by: Damian Holbrook, \"Glee Whiz\"","\"The Los Angeles Times\" (USA), 25 November 2010, pg. D18 - D19, by: Natalie Rotman, \"Neil Diamond opens up about his ''Dreams''\"","\"To allo vima\" (Greece), 7 October 2001, pg. 6,7, by: Dimitris Danikas","\"Zeilin\" (Netherlands), September 1986","''Cláudia Belchior'' (1994 - present); 1 child","''Inger Nørgaard'' (6 September 1980 - present)","''Majvor Andersson'' (1959 - 15 December 1999) (his death); 4 children","''Ryan Garing'' (9 August 2008 - present)","(1904). Stage Play: Business Is Business. Comedy/Drama. Written by ''Octave Mirbeau'' (qv). Translation by ''Robert Hichens'' (qv). Criterion Theatre: 19 Sep 1904- Nov 1904 (closing date unknown/57 performances). Cast: George Backus, ''Sheridan Block'' (qv), William H. Crane, George F. De Vere, Harriet Otis Dellenbaugh, W.H. Dupont, Emma Field, R.S. Fife, Isabel Garrison, ''Robert Paton Gibbs'' (qv), Katherine Grey, Harry Gwynette, Walter Hale, Josephine Mack, Harry Saint Maur, Frederick Maynard, ''Guy Nichols (I)'' (qv), Gabriel Ravenelle, Madeline Rives, Joseph Wheelock Jr. Produced by ''Charles Frohman'' (qv).","(1940s) Spoken-word album: Recorded a dramatic reading of ''Robert Browning (I)'' (qv)''s poem \"The Pied Piper of Hamelin\", for Decca Records (a two-record 78 RPM set), adapted by ''Edna Best'' (qv), with music by ''Victor Young (I)'' (qv). It has not yet appeared on CD.","(1967) Unsold pilot: Directed a comedy pilot for a proposed ABC series called \"Manley and the Mob\". The pilot starred ''Paul Lynde'' (qv) as a slow-witted private detective.","(1989 - 1994) Imprisoned for fraud (US$158 million)","(2002)In charge Programming section - Marrakech International Film Festival","(2009) Appeared in a TV commercial for Voices of Meningitis and online at voicesofmeningitis.org","(5 August 2000) Raced the Brickyard 400 in a car painted as a tribute to the 50th anniversary of Peanuts. Gordon''s \"copilots\" were Woodstock, Joe Cool and Snoopy''s WWI Flying Ace.","(January 2005) Spokesperson for Lakota pain reliever.","(November 29,1975 Evening) He performed in the ballet, \"Swan Lake,\" in a Royal Ballet production at the Royal Opera House in Covent Garden, London, England with Natalia Makarova, Anthony Dowell, Derek Rencher, Garry Grant, Dennis Griffith, Derek Deane, David Drew, Sandra Conley, Marguerite Porter, Hilary Tickner, Rosalyn Whitten, David Ashmole, Wayne Eagling, Christopher Carr, Lesley Collier, and Graham Fletcher in the cast.","1 November 1915","11 March 1888","13 January 1974","15 December 1948","16 September 1946","18 December 1963","19 October 1939",1964,"2 June 1977","21 April 1971","23 August 1943","25 April 1970","27 August 2010","29 April 1960","30 April 1978","4 June 1950","6 December 1980","8 August 1989","A beach-going type, who spends time surfing and enjoying time in the sun.","Album: \"Girls, Girls, Girls\" (1987/Elektra Records)","Appeared as himself in ''Non Stop'', a short filmed in 1968-69.","Attended Cornell University - was a double major in Mathematics and Film.","Bardoli, Gujarat, India","Bilingual: Hebrew and English.","Boulder, Colorado, USA","Bucharest, Romania","Cert X - The Music Of FILM4 FrightFest 2009 (Soundtrack CD)","Coached the Yankees in 1963, the Mets from 1965 to 1972, the Yankees again from 1976 to 1983, and the Astros from 1986 to 1989.","Crew Life: If anyone treated us today the way we were treated when the business started, there''d be a riot! In the 1960s and 70s we were just dogs to the American keys... We worked hard for our knowledge of filmmaking. Everyday on-set I''d write notes. So eventually we learned what all the equipment was for and what everyone on the crew did.","David Burner. _Herbert Hoover: A Public Life._ New York: Knopf, 1979.","Double D","England, UK (cancer)","Father of actress ''Viola Tree'' (qv) and grandfather of actor ''David Tree'' (qv).","Former football player for the New England Patriots and the Buffalo Bills.","Gave birth to her 1st child at age 29, a son Rafael Ritchie on September 5, 2011. Child''s father is her boyfriend (now fiancé), ''Guy Ritchie'' (qv).","Graduated from the University Of South Florida with a degree in Theatre 1992.","Haparanda, Norrbottens län, Sweden","Has two older brothers: Richard Whitney (b. November 24th 1944) and Brian Thomas (b. February 18th 1946), both born in Los Angeles.","He studied acting at University of Chile.","Her husband Manuel was the president of Benfica, a Portuguese football team.","His play, \"Court-Martial at Fort Devens\", at the Victory Gardens Theater in Chicago, Illinois was nominated for a 2007 ''Joseph Jefferson (I)'' (qv) Award for New Work.","I have the easiest job in the world. All I have to do is sing and play the guitar","In 2011 Joanna had a supporting role in the short film \"VR\" which made the official Selection at The Cannes Film Festival.","Is a vegetarian","Jazz Crazy (commissioned: treatment for a new Jazz Age musical)","Kaustav Sinha was born in the town of Chittaranjan (district: Burdwan), West Bengal, India. He is the son of Kalpana Sinha and Kallol Bikash Sinha. He has an elder sister, named Kankana Sinha. Kaustav moved to the city of Kolkata (Calcutta), India in 2004. He is a Digital Matte-Painter, Concept Artist and a Graphic Designer, and works for the Film Industry. Kaustav is the founder, owner and the director of the VFX post-production and Digital Matte-Painting freelance company, the Matte-Effect.","Laura Vázquez. \"Gente\". 1997","Long-time partner of ''Renate Krößner'' (qv).","Mamaroneck, New York, USA","Member of the Barefoot Theatre Company in New York City.","Montreal, Quebec, Canada","Music video: Emma Pollock - \"Paper And Glue\" (2007)","New York, USA (lung cancer)","Often appeared on the various radio & TV shows of New York City media couple \"Tex & Jinx\" (John Reagan ''Tex'' McCrary & Eugenia ''Jinx'' Lincoln Falkenberg). Waters appeared as a regular on the Tex & Jinx TV Show over WNBT in NYC starting January 29, 1954.","Oswego, New York, USA","Petra Feilen was educated in Stuttgart, where she performed for the Staatstheater as well as the Kleine Buehne. Other theatrical references are the Theater Lindenhof as well as the Waldau Theater Bremen. She has performed in TV and film productions such as Tatort (ARD), Der Mann von Gestern (ARD) and Glueckliche Tage. She was co-producer for a small dinner theatre ensemble in Bremen and was part of an English-speaking fringe ensemble until she decided to pursue film acting full time.","Popular leading man in 1940''s Hollywood who, with his suave demeanor, exotically handsome looks and well-modulated voice, was first called upon to portray mysterious or villainous characters. Soon he would be teamed with other \"exotics\" (e.g. ''Maria Montez (I)'' (qv) and ''Sabu (I)'' (qv)) in a series of escapist adventures, filmed in glorious Technicolor and set in lands of fable, which proved most popular with movie audiences of the World War II years. But with the end of the war, his career (like that of Montez) would decline. He ultimately returned to his city of birth to pursue opportunities in commercial photography.","Quebec City, Quebec, Canada","Resides in Prescott Valley, Arizona [2009].","San Bernadino, California, USA","She and her husband had one son and one daughter.","Sibilant voice","Son of ''Jayne Mansfield'' (qv) and ''Mickey Hargitay'' (qv). Half-brother of ''Jayne Marie Mansfield'' (qv) and ''Tony Cimber'' (qv) on his mother''s side and Tina Hargitay (b. 1949) on his father''s side.","Stage: Appeared in ''All the Living\" on Broadway.","Sunderland, Tyne-and-Wear, England, UK","TV commercial for The Los Angeles Mentoring Partnership (2005)","The Grapes of Wrath as Ruthie Joad directed by Claudio Raygoza, Ion Theatre Company","Timpas, Colorado, USA","Universal agreed to loan Hudson to his original studio Warner Bros. in exchange for the services of Warner contractee Virginia Mayo for the potboiler \"Congo Crossing.\".","Warsaw, Poland, Russian Empire [now Warsaw, Mazowieckie, Poland]","Was the original \"Roach Man\" at Universal Studios Florida -1993","Without dreams, we''re already dead.","Younger stepsister of ''Oliver Schell'' (qv).","_Blackadder Back & Forth (1999)_ (qv)","Ústí nad Labem, Czechoslovakia (now Czech Republic)"}', 'text'::regtype, -1), NULL, NULL, NULL);
